# Allowlist for scripts/forbid_bare_keepalive_family_invalidation.sh — every
# site where PASS 2 finds a cross-file `ref.invalidate(<keepAlive family>`
# that is NOT flagged as unsafe: either it IS the proven wasPinned-gated
# idiom's own `ref.invalidate` half (the eager `ref.read` half never matches
# PASS 2's pattern, so only the invalidate line needs listing), or it is
# self-key invalidation from the SAME still-mounted widget that is, at the
# moment it can fire, the family member's own ACTIVE watcher (listener count
# > 0, so `invalidateSelf()`'s `mayNeedDispose()` never queues disposal — the
# zero-listener precondition this whole bug class needs never occurs).
#
# Format: <repo-relative-path>:<line>   # reason
# Line-level (not file-level) on purpose — same reasoning as
# `.inline_fontsize_allow`: a whole-file exemption would let a genuinely new,
# unprotected cross-file invalidate slip in beside a reviewed one.
#
# --- Gated by the wasPinned + eager-read idiom (this track's fixes) ---------
lib/features/booking/application/booking_calendar_invalidation.dart:162  # invalidateBookingViewsAfterExternalDecline — wasPinned-gated (mirror of FIX B, this track, found via this gate and fixed with the identical idiom)
lib/features/booking/application/booking_calendar_invalidation.dart:287  # invalidateBookingViewsAfterProviderClose — FIX B (ITEM 1), wasPinned-gated via DayKeepAliveLru.contains
lib/features/booking/application/booking_calendar_invalidation.dart:426  # invalidateBookingViewsAfterBookingCreated — FIX (mobile-debugger, DayKeepAliveLru.contains-tautology fix, this track): now gated on DayKeepAliveLru.isWatched (backed by real onAddListener/onRemoveListener tracking in BookingsDayNotifier.build, not the old contains-against-its-own-enumeration check) — a genuinely-orphaned pinned member still gets the eager ref.read, a paused-but-watched one no longer does. Line shifted from 409 by this track's doc + isWatched-gate edit — no change to the allow-listed shape (still invalidate-then-conditionally-eager-read).
lib/features/booking/application/booking_calendar_invalidation.dart:535  # invalidateBookingsDayAfterAppointmentItemReschedule — pre-existing FIX A, wasPinned-gated via DayKeepAliveLru.contains (line shifted from 518 by the isWatched-fix's doc addition above it, this track — no logic change at this site)
#
# Phase 312 — three rows DELETED here (weekly_schedule_notifier.dart:134,
# master_schedule_screen.dart:534, master_schedule_screen.dart:682): all
# three sat in files this phase edits and already carried "Line renumbered
# from ..." scars from the PRIOR renumbering (phase 309/310). Rather than
# re-pin three new line numbers this phase would only re-break on its own
# next edit, each site now carries its reason as an inline
# `// keepalive-safe: <reason>` comment (verbatim) directly above its
# `ref.invalidate(...)` call — PASS 2 accepts either form, and a comment
# travels with the code so it can never de-sync again.
#
# --- Self-key retry / refresh, invalidating the SAME instance the SAME ------
# --- still-mounted widget is ACTIVELY watching in the SAME build -----------
# Each of these fires from inside the identical `Consumer`/`State.build` that
# `ref.watch`es this EXACT family member on the line(s) directly above it —
# the widget IS that member's live listener at the moment the button can be
# tapped, so listener count is never zero and the disposal race this gate
# exists for cannot occur. None of these swap to a DIFFERENT key first (that
# swap — a rail tap, a sort toggle, a week page — is what creates the
# pinned-but-unwatched element the fixes above protect).
